abstract: "Open-source software ecosystem comprising: (1) ScarCodec v6.3.0 (Biorthogonal), a Zero-PyTorch (NumPy + multithreaded C99/SIMD) library, CRC32 mmap binary format (.scar), and Zarr/numcodecs plugin (ScarZarrCodec) delivering 10.5x-54.1x IEEE-754 scientific compression (D4 VQ4, 1.000 bpw Conway-Sloane O(8) Gosset E8 at 44.4-72.5 MB/s, and 3D Tucker), 0.376 us O(1) 64-float random block reads, biorthogonal smooth-shock-lattice decoupling (+8.56 dB on Mw 9.1 Tohoku, -27.06% IEC 50 uV ECG bytes), Behrens-Scharf oblique interference nulling (P_biorth), 29-decade deterministic L_inf error bounds, and 34,816 B (Delta=0 B) dual associative anomaly telemetry validated across 16 SHA-256-verified files from 10 public archives and modern 2026 SOTA (SZ3, SPERR, Blosc2, CCSDS-121, Frequent Directions); and (2) ScarField v7.5-Fused / ScarNativeLM / MoS foundations across native and WebGPU runtimes."
